  "handoff": {
    "summary": "{\"capsule\":{\"case_sha256_canonical_encoded\":\"912ce6efad9bde5c34d99f398c74493621d8359504b2f7dc437e176113fcd56c\",\"pools\":[{\"candidates\":[{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"P1\",\"op\":\"tap\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"P2\",\"op\":\"tap\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"P1\",\"op\":\"pull\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"P2\",\"op\":\"pull\",\"tick\":8}],\"burden\":\"Four operator ticks and two impacts; H stays assembled. Removal needs two separate pulls. No new component or restoration action.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"One pin alone supplies only 2; either pull before the final required hold boundary would reduce capacity below 4. Tapping with detached H is unsupported.\",\"id\":\"AC20-PRE-implementation-P1\",\"lineage\":\"Initial precursor from task facts J03,J04 and the explicit conventional archive J10; no received proposal or analog source.\",\"mechanism\":\"Intact H installs P1 and P2; their capacities add to 4. Pulls remove their contributions individually.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled proposal: 4 units from boundary 2 until boundary 8, then 2 until boundary 9, then no installed pins. The conventional precursor is not locally original.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J04\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J11\",\"J12\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"install\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"insert\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"withdraw\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"remove\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six operator ticks including optional hammer restoration; zero impacts. H cannot tap while S is deployed. V installation alone provides no stated retention, so all three setup actions must finish by boundary 3.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Leaving H intact denies the required free S. Delayed insertion misses tick 3. Pins or another non-pin assembly cannot supplement the sleeve. Skipping withdrawal prevents the specified release sequence.\",\"id\":\"AC20-PRE-implementation-P2\",\"lineage\":\"Initial construction derived solely from J03 and J06; it has not been revised by assistance. Full precursor schedule preserved.\",\"mechanism\":\"Detach frees S; installed V plus inserted S supplies min(4,4)=4. Withdrawal removes the active stem contribution, removal clears V, and final assembly restores H using free M and S.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled proposal: 4 units beginning boundary 3 through boundary 7; withdrawal completes at 8, V removal at 9, and H restoration at 10. Compared with the two-pin precursor, impacts fall from two to zero while operator actions increase from four to six. Real-world novelty is undetermined.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J06\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J11\",\"J12\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"place\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"route\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"unroute\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"lift\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six operator ticks including optional H restoration; zero impacts. M is occupied through boundary 9, keeping H unavailable for tapping. Both setup actions after disassembly and both release actions are necessary.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Placement alone or routing alone does not establish retention. H cannot remain assembled while M is placed. Omitting unroute or lift leaves the prescribed release incomplete.\",\"id\":\"AC20-PRE-implementation-P3\",\"lineage\":\"Initial construction from J03 and J07, independently generated within the implementation concern; no other investigator, proposal, or analog was consulted.\",\"mechanism\":\"Detach frees M; place M then route L supplies min(4,4)=4 through their joint assembly. Unroute ends retention and lift frees M; free M and S allow assembly at tick 9.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled proposal: 4 units from boundary 3 through boundary 7; unroute completes at 8, lift at 9, and H restoration at 10. Relative to the sleeve, the occupied hammer component changes from S to M while action count and modeled capacity match. No measured mechanics or global originality claim.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J07\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J11\",\"J12\"]}],\"handoff_residue\":\"The non-pin setups have no spare setup tick before boundary 3 and displace hammer availability. Added reassembly is a burden choice, not a hard requirement. Equal modeled capacity does not make sleeve and loop resource occupancy interchangeable.\",\"job_id\":\"AC20-PRE-implementation\",\"raw_sha256\":\"7ece3f059b6428dedec4b9f9af29df47f57250487e86e0ce2d357a8c12a18edd\",\"source_limits\":[\"All outcomes are finite-model proposals pending root replay, not measured physics or final self-grades.\",\"J10 names two-pin and clip constructions as conventional; absence of sleeve or loop from that archive cannot prove wider novelty.\",\"Q theta remains unknown in {0,4}. No unconditional Q-only construction is advanced; measurement itself creates no retention.\",\"No changed impact ladder, adhesive, welding, sustained manual support, extra resource, or unlisted operation is used.\"]},{\"candidates\":[{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"C\",\"op\":\"install\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"C\",\"op\":\"remove\",\"tick\":7}],\"burden\":\"Two operator actions and zero taps. H remains intact and its parts remain available. No operator action is needed during ticks 3-6. C is occupied from boundary 3 until boundary 8 and cannot serve another location.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Installation completing after boundary 3 misses required retention; removal completing within the hold window breaks service. Failing to remove C by boundary 10 breaks release.\",\"id\":\"PRE-SVC-C\",\"lineage\":\"Initial precursor independently constructed from the current J0 facts; conventional clip construction explicitly acknowledged by J10.\",\"mechanism\":\"install(C) completes at boundary 3 and supplies 4 units. remove(C) at tick 7 completes at boundary 8, removing the sole retainer and permitting separation.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled: retention is 4 at each required tick; all installed retainers are gone by boundary 8. Upkeep requires no stipulated intervention during holding; post-service C is free and H is intact. Compared with the other two candidates, fewer actions and no H disassembly are required. No wear, inspection interval or reliability claim follows from the axioms; local originality is excluded by J10.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J05\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"install\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"insert\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"withdraw\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"remove\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six operator actions including asset restoration; zero taps. S is occupied in V until boundary 8, so H cannot support tapping while disassembled. M remains free. V remains installed until boundary 9. No intervention is required during holding.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Intact H leaves S unavailable for insertion. Omitting withdrawal prevents valid sleeve removal; omitting remove(V) leaves an installed retainer at the deadline. Earlier withdrawal would interrupt the hold window.\",\"id\":\"PRE-SVC-SV\",\"lineage\":\"Initial precursor independently constructed solely from J03 and J06 under the current service contract; no proposal or analog received.\",\"mechanism\":\"detach(H) frees S at boundary 1; V installs at boundary 2; S insertion completes at boundary 3 with min(4,4)=4 retention. Withdrawal completes at boundary 8, removing retention; sleeve removal completes at boundary 9. Assembly restores H at boundary 10.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled: 4 units throughout ticks 3-6; retention ends at boundary 8 and the last installed retainer is removed by boundary 9, permitting separation. Upkeep after release returns S and M to intact H by boundary 10 and leaves V free. Compared with C, this needs four additional actions and temporarily removes hammer availability. Reassembly restores tool configuration without creating retention. Wear, jamming, repeated-cycle endurance and field maintainability remain unknown; archive absence alone does not establish broader novelty.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J06\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"place\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"route\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"unroute\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"lift\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six operator actions including restoration, zero taps. M is occupied until boundary 9, L until boundary 8; H is unavailable for tapping while detached. S remains free. No manual support or hold-period action is assumed.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Placing M alone gives no stated 4-unit assembly. Routing late misses boundary 3. Unrouting alone does not complete recovery: lift(M) remains required, and assembly cannot precede freeing M.\",\"id\":\"PRE-SVC-ML\",\"lineage\":\"Initial precursor independently constructed solely from J03 and J07 under current J0 facts; no analog bank or other role output exposed.\",\"mechanism\":\"Detach completes at boundary 1, placement at boundary 2 and routing at boundary 3. The conjunction supplies min(4,4)=4. Unrouting completes at boundary 8, then lifting completes at boundary 9; assembly completes at boundary 10.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled: 4 units at ticks 3-6; unrouting ends retention at boundary 8 and lifting clears the remaining installed assembly component at boundary 9, permitting separation. Upkeep restores intact H by boundary 10 and frees L. The action count matches S/V, but the occupied hammer component and release order differ: L must be unrouted before M is lifted. No elastic behavior, inspection rule, fatigue resistance or physical advantage over S/V is established. This is an alternate stipulated mechanism, not demonstrated field novelty.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J07\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\"]}],\"handoff_residue\":\"Clip achieves the required modeled service with two actions; the other candidates use six to restore H. Withdrawal or unrouting ends retention before final component recovery. No stipulated wear model exists. The original invalid service remains invalid; this fresh precursor neither imports its unseen contents nor retroactively repairs its verdict.\",\"job_id\":\"COV-AC20-PRE-service\",\"raw_sha256\":\"dfc13c407de2fd6bb9f79d626cdd04d2700041f05a0134036ac2ad0dfdf09dde\",\"source_limits\":[\"Only literal J01-J12 facts used; no direct input jobs exist, so all input_job_refs are empty.\",\"All candidate outcomes are modeled predictions, not observed execution or self-grading. Root replays action effects.\",\"Service requirement and release deadline are unchanged. No declared ladder cell or impact-budget change is made.\",\"Q theta cannot be assumed; measurement creates no retention. No Q construction is claimed.\",\"Upkeep predictions cover resource recovery and tool reassembly only; no wear or recurring maintenance axiom is available.\",\"No claim about an unseen original schedule is invented; the original invalid service remains invalid.\"]},{\"candidates\":[{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"C\",\"op\":\"install\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"C\",\"op\":\"remove\",\"tick\":7}],\"burden\":\"Two actions, zero impacts; H intact, C occupied boundaries 3-8. No holding-period work.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Late install misses boundary 3; early removal breaks holding; omission breaks release.\",\"id\":\"LS0-C\",\"lineage\":\"Received construction with unchanged actions; routed interpretation only. Exact precursor and source edges are preserved in operation_trace and handoff.\",\"mechanism\":\"Installed C alone provides 4; removal clears the sole retainer.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled proposal: 4 at ticks 3-6, C free by 8. Four fewer actions than either restored-component alternative; conventional archive status unchanged.\",\"source_refs\":[\"AM\",\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J05\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"install\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"insert\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"withdraw\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"remove\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six actions, zero impacts; H unavailable until 10, S occupied until 8, V installed until 9. M stays free.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Intact H prevents insertion; delayed insertion misses hold; omitted withdrawal/removal leaves recovery incomplete.\",\"id\":\"LS0-SV\",\"lineage\":\"Received construction with unchanged actions; routed interpretation only. Exact precursor and source edges are preserved in operation_trace and handoff.\",\"mechanism\":\"Detach frees S; V plus inserted S supplies min(4,4)=4; withdrawal then removal clears V. Assembly restores H.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled proposal: retention starts at 3, ends at 8; retainers clear at 9, optional H restoration at 10. Different component occupation from M/L, no new source-induced mechanism.\",\"source_refs\":[\"AM\",\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J06\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"place\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"route\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"unroute\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"lift\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six actions, zero impacts; H unavailable until 10, M occupied until 9, L until 8. S stays free.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Placement alone supplies no stated retention; omitted unroute/lift breaks recovery; assembling before M is free is unsupported.\",\"id\":\"LS0-ML\",\"lineage\":\"Received construction with unchanged actions; routed interpretation only. Exact precursor and source edges are preserved in operation_trace and handoff.\",\"mechanism\":\"Detach frees M; placement plus routing L supplies min(4,4)=4. Unroute then lift clears assembly; reassembly restores H.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled proposal: retention starts at 3, ends at 8; assembly clears at 9, optional restoration at 10. Equal action count to S/V does not equal component interchangeability.\",\"source_refs\":[\"AM\",\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J07\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\"]}],\"handoff_residue\":\"Sleeve and loop exhaust setup time before 3 and displace H. H restoration is optional extra work. Clip and pins are conventional. Shared interpretation cannot establish newly discovered mechanisms, independent investigators/data, global novelty, real mechanics or source benefit. First invalid route and service observations stay invalid; this later comparison cannot restore gated first-study conclusions.\",\"job_id\":\"COV-SOURCE-LATER-SHARED-route0\",\"raw_sha256\":\"91f35190a2d819a30424d89e93d9bb557dbbb4021e7fb8a41b3e3462a4593769\",\"source_limits\":[\"Finite-model proposals pending root replay; supplied precursor replay observations are not current execution.\",\"No mechanical transfer from AM; no Q assumption, new resource, primitive, combination, or impact-ladder change.\",\"Shared synthetic source and mixed precursor times limit independence and causal efficacy claims.\",\"Only literal packet used; no invalid first-route output inspected or rewritten.\"]},{\"candidates\":[{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"C\",\"op\":\"install\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"C\",\"op\":\"remove\",\"tick\":7}],\"burden\":\"Two operator actions, zero impacts, H stays intact; C occupied boundaries 3-8.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Late installation misses tick 3; premature removal breaks holding; missing removal violates boundary 10.\",\"id\":\"LSH1-C\",\"lineage\":\"Received PRE-SVC-C, unchanged after AM exposure.\",\"mechanism\":\"C alone supplies 4; removing C completes recovery. AM prompts outcome and burden scrutiny; J05 supplies mechanics.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled proposal: 4 at required ticks; C removed at boundary 8. Conventional per J10; no assisted capacity gain.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J05\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\",\"AM\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"install\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"insert\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"withdraw\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"remove\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six actions, zero impacts; S occupied through 8, H unavailable until restoration; three setup ticks leave no slack.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Intact H denies free S; late insertion or early withdrawal violates holding; omitted V removal leaves retainer.\",\"id\":\"LSH1-SV\",\"lineage\":\"Received implementation-P2 and PRE-SVC-SV, identical unchanged schedules.\",\"mechanism\":\"Detached S inserted in V supplies min(4,4); withdrawal ends retention, sleeve removal clears assembly.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled proposal: 4 begins boundary 3; withdrawal completes 8, V removal 9, optional H restoration 10.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J06\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\",\"AM\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"place\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"route\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"unroute\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"lift\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six actions, zero impacts; M occupied through 9, L through 8, H unavailable until restoration.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Placement alone supplies no retention; delayed routing misses tick 3; omitted lift fails complete recovery.\",\"id\":\"LSH1-ML\",\"lineage\":\"Received implementation-P3 and PRE-SVC-ML, identical unchanged schedules.\",\"mechanism\":\"Detached M plus routed L jointly supply min(4,4); unroute must precede lift.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled proposal: 4 begins boundary 3; unroute completes 8, lift 9, optional H restoration 10.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J07\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\",\"AM\"]}],\"handoff_residue\":\"Supplied first COV-AC20-SHARED-route0/route1 observations remain terminal invalid: Exact role JSON keys required; coordinator observed actual_FINAL, not independent platform attestation. Their raw hashes remain 9201e47ab7005fb94aaa116058ecd0b83429328c968478219f4b0f9d9cee340c and ffd03ec747a7d97cc12c57775a0943f869409ba0c1c5c1ea25e6c9da867c0f3a. Prior failure/gates remain unavailable. No invalid files inspected. Recovery differs from retention ending; hammer restoration is optional burden. No wear model, empirical independence, new mechanism, or assistance benefit is established.\",\"job_id\":\"COV-SOURCE-LATER-SHARED-route1\",\"raw_sha256\":\"d302d77652be1365bb789913fa31d5452078ba136f39067105b9da75a097e664\",\"source_limits\":[\"Stipulated finite model only; root replay is required, with no final self-grade or measured physics.\",\"No wider novelty or global optimality follows; C and two-pin are archived conventional constructions.\",\"Shared seed, distinct routes and equal-union information are different comparisons; one synthetic body is not independent empirical corroboration.\",\"Original and later precursor draws are mixed; this later chain cannot regrade the gated first study or repair invalid outputs.\"]}],\"source_routes\":[{\"forwarded_source_provenance\":{\"AC20-PRE-implementation\":{\"scope\":\"Literal received role data or selected summary only; original source bytes are not thereby supplied.\",\"source_ids\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J04\",\"J06\",\"J07\",\"J08\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J11\",\"J12\"]},\"COV-AC20-PRE-service\":{\"scope\":\"Literal received role data or selected summary only; original source bytes are not thereby supplied.\",\"source_ids\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J05\",\"J06\",\"J07\",\"J08\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J11\",\"J12\"]}},\"job_id\":\"COV-SOURCE-LATER-SHARED-route0\",\"payload_sha256\":\"aeec1ae5fd9b68ae03e4d4efb940c5b54cf04505bca6570df503c8e65b2bde38\",\"source_banks\":[{\"body_sha256_canonical_encoded\":\"b3cdd1beca1904d3ae4a30f08c0c3439cc26a2d1c1dd28b42831c659821c7c40\",\"original_file_sha256\":\"5055c0b93d9a7c569f007ae97ad03033274e0e19645a74f0eb6a6a14a98494ec\",\"original_path\":\"/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/runs/2026-10-10-composed-ten/inputs/cases.json\",\"original_selector\":\"DEV\",\"selector_key\":\"route_material\",\"source_id\":\"AM\"}],\"source_exposure_manifest\":{\"distinct_empirical_datasets\":false,\"literal_bytes\":10288,\"selectors\":[\"route_material\"],\"unique_bodies\":1}},{\"forwarded_source_provenance\":{\"AC20-PRE-implementation\":{\"scope\":\"Literal received role data or selected summary only; original source bytes are not thereby supplied.\",\"source_ids\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J04\",\"J06\",\"J07\",\"J08\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J11\",\"J12\"]},\"COV-AC20-PRE-service\":{\"scope\":\"Literal received role data or selected summary only; original source bytes are not thereby supplied.\",\"source_ids\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J05\",\"J06\",\"J07\",\"J08\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J11\",\"J12\"]}},\"job_id\":\"COV-SOURCE-LATER-SHARED-route1\",\"payload_sha256\":\"66d0254f1a45898980f0246ca6646527cea979933727fee09f9943f07e75c4f0\",\"source_banks\":[{\"body_sha256_canonical_encoded\":\"b3cdd1beca1904d3ae4a30f08c0c3439cc26a2d1c1dd28b42831c659821c7c40\",\"original_file_sha256\":\"5055c0b93d9a7c569f007ae97ad03033274e0e19645a74f0eb6a6a14a98494ec\",\"original_path\":\"/home/vlad_/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab/docs/proposals/hammer-bias-strategies/novelty/runs/2026-10-10-composed-ten/inputs/cases.json\",\"original_selector\":\"DEV\",\"selector_key\":\"route_material\",\"source_id\":\"AM\"}],\"source_exposure_manifest\":{\"distinct_empirical_datasets\":false,\"literal_bytes\":10288,\"selectors\":[\"route_material\"],\"unique_bodies\":1}}]},\"construction\":\"Fresh builder receives this summary only and may construct at most one candidate, using an existing supported family without any novelty obligation. Keep J0 unchanged: two aligned panels need at least 4 units at ticks 3,4,5,6; permit separation with every installed retainer removed by boundary 10; no damage, discard, substitution or outside resource. One operator performs at most one action per integer tick, completing at the next boundary; resources cannot occupy two places. H initially intact; all other identities free. Exact action objects have only tick, op, arg. Choose one construction, never combine alternatives. Preferred low-burden received construction: tick2 install C, tick7 remove C; install supplies 4 at boundary3, removal clears C at boundary8. H stays intact; two actions, zero impacts; conventional per J10. Preserved S/V alternative: tick0 detach H, tick1 install V, tick2 insert S,V, tick7 withdraw S,V, tick8 remove V, tick9 assemble H. Detachment frees S; installed V with S supplies min(4,4)=4 from boundary3 until withdrawal completes8. V alone supplies no stipulated retention; final removal completes9, optional reassembly10. Six actions, zero impacts; S occupied until8, V until9, H unavailable until10; M stays free. Preserved M/L alternative: tick0 detach H, tick1 place M, tick2 route L, tick7 unroute L, tick8 lift M, tick9 assemble H. Detachment frees M; placement plus routed L supplies min(4,4)=4 from boundary3 until unrouting completes8. Both placement and routing are required; unroute precedes lift, which clears M at9; optional H restoration completes10. Six actions, zero impacts; L occupied until8, M until9; S stays free. Frozen intact-H reference in the capsule: tick0 tap P1, tick1 tap P2, tick7 pull P1, tick8 pull P2. Each pin contributes2; intact H is required for tap. Four actions, two impacts at unchanged b=2; pins clear9. Do not build a fourth exchange candidate from this reference. Only one non-pin assembly may be installed and it cannot mix with pins. No sustained manual support, adhesive, welding, elastic extrapolation, new parts or unlisted operation. Q supplies theta in {0,4}; no theta assumption or analog-derived capacity. A refusal to assert Q sufficiency is useful and permitted. Preserve the complete capsule and these limits through the builder handoff, including all twelve precursor candidates and each source-route identity. Root replays action effects; do not self-grade. Existing schedules are received mechanisms, not additions discovered by exchange. Earlier incomplete handoffs and first grades stay unchanged.\",\"audit\":\"Actual joined-pool inspection: twelve entries comprise four action/mechanism families: one two-pin reference, three clip entries, four S/V entries and four M/L entries. Graph for intact-H pins: J03+J04+J10 -> AC20-PRE-implementation-P1; it remains a frozen comparator. Graph for clip: J05+J10 -> PRE-SVC-C -> LS0-C and LSH1-C -> exchange C. Graph for sleeve: J03+J06 -> AC20-PRE-implementation-P2 and PRE-SVC-SV -> LS0-SV and LSH1-SV -> exchange SV. Graph for loop: J03+J07 -> AC20-PRE-implementation-P3 and PRE-SVC-ML -> LS0-ML and LSH1-ML -> exchange ML. Initial pools claim no analog exposure. Forwarded implementation source IDs omit J05; forwarded service source IDs omit J04; their union and the current common case cover J01-J12. Both later route identities attach AM, selector route_material, original_selector DEV, to reconsidering preferred means and auditing intermediate retention versus complete recovery. Both supplied source banks have identical body and original-file hashes and manifests: one unique body, 10288 literal bytes, distinct_empirical_datasets false. These are route-reported exposures and interpretations, not direct AM original-body exposure by this exchange. The capsule preserves both route payload hashes, original source selector/path/hash, full pool raw hashes, and each original candidate source_refs/lineage/limits without alteration. Contrary dependency: intact H is necessary for tap under J04, but S/V and M/L specifically need detached/free S or M under J03/J06/J07; therefore intact-H preference cannot be promoted to a universal retention requirement. C directly supplies4 under J05 without either impact or detachment. Contrary to an interpretation that the joined schedules omit recovery, every received S/V schedule withdraws then removes V, and every M/L schedule unrouts via unroute then lifts M. They already clear retainers at9 and optionally restore H at10; no contract break has been found to repair. Qualified usefulness comparison within this pool: C has two actions, zero impacts and intact H; pins have four actions and two impacts; S/V and M/L have six actions, zero impacts and displaced H availability. All supplied replays report4 at required ticks and no errors, but this role does not replay them. The S/V and M/L families have real component/sequence differences despite equal action counts and capacity: S stays occupied to8 versus M to9, V removal versus M lifting, and the other hammer component stays free. They preserve mechanism diversity, but no superior current service outcome over the available C is established. Unresolved method tension: retaining distinct pre-existing component mechanisms and full provenance increases transmitted text while routed candidate schedules add no new family. The capsule can support a fidelity audit but cannot attribute pool quality, independence, novelty or efficacy to shared routing. No supported new mechanical opening follows from AM, and no axiom contradiction is identified. Missing wear/endurance data and Q theta are uncertainties, not free design variables. Previous invalid route/service observations and unavailable first-study gates remain as received; this later transmission cannot regrade them.\",\"limits\":[\"This is a separate prospective provenance-transmission exchange. Earlier incomplete handoffs, raw outputs and first grades remain unchanged; none of the missing earlier exchange/builder content is supplied or reconstructed.\",\"All predictions are stipulated finite-model claims pending root replay. Supplied replay records are packet observations, not execution by this role, measured physics or a final self-grade.\",\"The 10000-word allowance supports literal provenance transport only. Six slots, agent counts and output word caps do not establish matched compute or efficacy.\",\"All twelve precursor candidate objects, source limits, pool hashes, route identities, selectors and source hashes are copied unchanged inside handoff.summary.capsule. Hashes and manifest values are supplied identifiers, not independently verified original source bytes.\",\"Only this literal exchange packet was read. No new source bank, web, memory, helper, fresh builder, earlier-output inspection or retry is used. AM evidence here is forwarded role data and source metadata; original source path is not opened.\",\"Clip and two-pin mechanisms are conventional under J10. Sleeve and loop are already proposed target mechanisms; neither routed repetition nor this exchange establishes novelty, independent empirical corroboration or assistance benefit.\",\"Shared source, concern routes and equal-union information are different comparisons. Original implementation and later service draws are mixed, and precursor source coverage differs at J04 versus J05.\",\"Q theta remains unknown in {0,4}; measurement creates no retention. No Q-only guarantee, unlisted primitive, new identity, pin/non-pin mix, second non-pin assembly, outside support or changed impact ladder is introduced.\",\"H restoration is optional additional work. Retention ending and removing every installed retainer are separate obligations. No wear, repeated-cycle reliability, future workload or physical advantage is specified.\"]}",
    "residue": "No previous incomplete exchange or builder output was supplied. This transmission must not repair or regrade them. The repeated source routes do not supply new candidate families. C is lowest burden within the received pool; SV/ML retain distinct dependencies but displace H and exhaust setup time. Every received release sequence is already complete; restoration is optional. All inconvenient details and literal lineage are explicitly included in summary."
  },
